4429.sol:
For the salt of type $A_2 B$, solubility product

$\left(K_{\mathrm{sp}$}\right)=x^x $\cdot$y^y $\cdot$S^{x+y}

where, $x and y$ are the number of moles of A and B$ respectively.

S=\text{ solubility. }Thus, $\quad K_${\mathrm{sp}}$=2^2 \times 1^1 \cdot S^{2+1} \Rightarrow K_${\mathrm{sp}}$=4 S^3$
Given, $K_${\mathrm{sp}}$ for A_2 B=3.2 \times 10^{-11} $\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore& 3.2 \times10^{-11}=4 S³ \\
\text{ or, }& S³=\frac{3.2}{4} \times10^{-11}=8 \times10^{-12} \\
\text{ Thus, }& S=2 \times10^{-4}
\end{array}$

Hence, option (b) is the correct answer.

