60550.sol:
Given, $f(x)=\log (1+x)-\frac{2 x}{2+x} \begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad$ f^{\prime}(x) &=$\frac{1}{1+x}-\frac{(2+x) \cdot 2-2 x}{(2+x)^{2}}$\\
&=$\frac{x^{2}}{(1+x)(x+2)^{2}}
\end{aligned}$ Clearly, $f^{\prime}(x) > 0$ for all $x > 0$. Hence, $f(x)$ is increasing on $(0, \infty)$.

